No dark theme is planned for MVP. User-specific theme settings are not necessary for the current audience and would expand the accessibility test surface.

### Typography

- Primary: locally served Irancell, weights 400/500/700/800.
- Fallback: Tahoma, Arial, sans-serif.
- Body: 16px minimum on mobile; line-height 1.8 for Persian readability.
- Labels and supporting text: never below 13px.
- Hero display: responsive clamp, maximum approximately 64px.
- Numbers/case references: maintain readable direction with `dir="ltr"` where needed.

### Spacing and shape

- Spacing scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 72.
- Controls: minimum 44px touch height.
- Input radius: 12px.
- Card radius: 20px.
- Hero/section container radius: up to 30px only for major authored surfaces.
- Shadows: one low-elevation shadow; borders do most structural work.

### Layout

- Content width: 1180px maximum with 20px mobile gutters.
- Public hero: asymmetric two-column layout, copy dominant, service route visual secondary.
- Service cards: three columns ≥ 900px, single column on narrow screens.
- Intake: one main form column plus a sticky trust/summary rail on desktop; one column on mobile.
- Staff console: navigation rail + content; operational cards/tables, no public hero styling.

## Component rules

### Buttons

- One primary action per surface.
- Primary: solid brand background, white text.
- Secondary: surface with line border.
- Tertiary: text link with visible hover/focus.
- Destructive actions use danger styling and a clear object label.
- Disable only when action cannot run; preserve readable contrast and explain why where non-obvious.

### Forms

- Use `<form novalidate>` and provide controlled client-side messages while preserving server validation.
- Labels always remain visible; placeholders show examples only.
- Required state uses text or `aria-describedby`, not an asterisk alone.
- Errors appear directly below the field, update `aria-invalid`, and are summarised/focused on submit when multiple fields fail.
- Textareas are manually resizable vertically.
- Persian mobile number input uses `inputmode="tel"`, accepts Persian/Arabic digits, and normalises on submission.
- Budget is a range preference with “مایلم تلفنی مطرح کنم”; it never promises a treatment price.

### OPG upload

- Explain accepted formats and maximum size before selection.
- Support click/keyboard and drag/drop; the native input remains operable.
- Show selected name, human-readable size, validation/scan stage and explicit remove/retry actions.
- Do not display a successful upload until the server has persisted it; do not display “safe” until scanning approves it.
- Preview only safe, supported image types. PDF is represented by file metadata unless a safe renderer is available.
- Consent is separate from selecting a file and never pre-checked.

### Service cards

Each card contains: icon, plain-language service name, one-line scope, availability label and action. Selected cards use border, background and checkmark—not colour alone.

### Trust boundary

The clinician limitation appears:

- under the OPG service description;
- next to consent/review before submission;
- on the case receipt;
- on every preliminary assessment.

It should be calm and legible, not hidden in a footer or styled as alarming legal boilerplate.

## Content principles

- Use “راهنمایی و هماهنگی” for Royadarman actions.
- Use “بررسی اولیه توسط دندانپزشک دارای مجوز” for OPG review.
- Use “گزینه‌های متناسب با نیاز و بودجه اعلام‌شده” rather than “cheapest” or guaranteed “best.”
- Say “درخواست” until a human confirms a visit; do not say “نوبت قطعی.”
- Say “پوشش فعلی: شهر تهران” on every home-service entry point.
- Do not prefix the owner's name with “دکتر” unless a verified professional credential later supports it.
- Avoid urgency theatre. “24-hour support” means availability of intake/support, not continuous emergency dentistry.

## Responsive and accessibility requirements

- Test at 320, 375, 768, 1024 and 1440 CSS pixels.
- All flows keyboard-operable in logical RTL order.
- Skip link, landmarks and one H1 per page.
- Focus indicator at least 3px and visible on all surfaces.
- Minimum AA contrast for text and controls.
- Honour `prefers-reduced-motion`; no critical information depends on animation.
- Do not lock zoom or use horizontal scrolling for patient forms.
- Tables gain labels/card layout on small screens rather than becoming unreadable.
- Status and error copy is announced with appropriate live-region politeness.
- Uploaded-file remove/retry controls have explicit accessible names.

## Motion

- 160–220ms ease-out for hover, disclosure and panel transitions.
- A subtle one-time path draw may appear in the hero.
- Upload progress may animate only while real work is occurring.
- Reduced-motion mode removes path/progress motion and uses instant state changes.

## Assets

Use authored SVG shapes/icons and local fonts for MVP. No stock photo is required: an image of a dentist could incorrectly imply that the owner or a specific clinician provides all care. When real partner photography is introduced, obtain usage rights and caption it accurately.

## Verification checklist

- Copy reflects coordination, Tehran home service and licensed OPG review.
- Owner is not described or visually represented as a doctor.
- Native semantics remain intact under authored styling.
- All form/upload success, error, empty, offline/retry and pending states exist.
- Focus, keyboard and reduced-motion behaviour pass.
- No placeholder `href="#"`, browser alert/confirm/prompt, remote hotlinked asset or public upload URL.
- Strict premium UI audit passes with no critical issue.
- Browser verification includes console, network, RTL layout and mobile viewport checks.
